cy_key": "ci-fix-money-half-even-08d3cd5986"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 12695, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01MJQkUGN386NgdpuvDUUEnk", "tool": "trigger_ci", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-half-even-08d3cd5986", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 12695, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01MJQkUGN386NgdpuvDUUEnk", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 15255, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Po18s3Wok9Rd2gpTG14Z4q", "tool": "wait_for_ci", "args": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 372695, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Po18s3Wok9Rd2gpTG14Z4q", "tool": "wait_for_ci", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 372695, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Po18s3Wok9Rd2gpTG14Z4q", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 378427, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01LrkHVADxrjoLzBtDmU9T7v", "tool": "open_pr", "args": {"head": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring already says HALF_EVEN.\n\nChange: switch `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 379327, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01LrkHVADxrjoLzBtDmU9T7v", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 379327, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01LrkHVADxrjoLzBtDmU9T7v", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 383525, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it should use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN). So `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of the `2.66` that `tests/test_money.py` expects.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That's the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101).\n\nI haven't merged it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval. I also couldn't check the rule itself: looking up FIN-212 returned \"unknown advisory,\" so I went by the test and the docstring.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017dr1xLbvYbRqbBCbXjVAWA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01KTzTxPtY9JAyu9xUcn2SEt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01VR5S4e2g4MUJDVj1QZE3HE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_016tyo3DXxTuzZpvu4zU5DMm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VAzWgQ1Litaq9bw96Ewxbo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money, per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01MJQkUGN386NgdpuvDUUEnk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-half-even-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Po18s3Wok9Rd2gpTG14Z4q", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01LrkHVADxrjoLzBtDmU9T7v", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring already says HALF_EVEN.\n\nChange: switch `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it should use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN). So `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of the `2.66` that `tests/test_money.py` expects.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That's the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101).\n\nI haven't merged it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval. I also couldn't check the rule itself: looking up FIN-212 returned \"unknown advisory,\" so I went by the test and the docstring.", "type": "text"}]}]}